Original commit body from 291c9c3:

Migrate 45 language analyzers to use the shared NameResolver/SymbolResolver/
ListNameResolver framework for cross-file symbol resolution. This ensures
consistent call resolution patterns across all languages.

Key changes:
- All analyzers now use two-pass analysis (symbols first, then edges)
- Call edges use resolver.lookup() for callee resolution
- Resolved calls get confidence 0.85 * lookup_confidence
- Unresolved calls get external IDs with confidence 0.70

New call resolution added to:
- HLSL: Cross-file function call tracking for DirectX shaders
- Nix: Function call tracking in Nix expressions
- Starlark: Function call tracking in Bazel/Buck files
- PowerShell: Migrated from synthetic IDs to proper resolution

